In one week, students at a school in Coimbatore noted five things:
(i) the juice of a raw tamarind tasted sour;
(ii) the puddles on the playground dried up on a hot, sunny afternoon;
(iii) a strip of aluminium foil made the lamp in a circuit glow but a plastic straw did not;
(iv) the wax of a lit candle melted;
(v) the iron gate of the school turned rusty after the rains.
For each observation, name the topic of the chapter's tour it belongs to and give the chapter's link in one line.
